          "axis": "consistency",
          "severity": "major",
          "field": "household_units",
          "problem": "The entry mixes two forms in one ingredient: piece=2g refers to a cinnamon stick (whole bark), while tsp=2.5g and tbsp=7g refer to cinnamon powder (notes explicitly say 'cinnamon powder'). canonical_form says 'cinnamon stick'. A cinnamon stick and cinnamon powder have different bulk densities, different culinary uses (sticks for biryani/garam masala simmering, powder for desserts/baking), and recipes call for them by different names. Recipe authors will be confused about which form they're specifying.",
          "suggested_fix": "Split into two ingredients: 'cinnamon stick' (with piece unit only) and 'cinnamon powder' (with tsp/tbsp units). Alternative: keep as one entry but rename to 'cinnamon' (no form) and clarify each unit's form in the notes. Splitting is cleaner."
